      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an experienced HR recruiter.\nYour task is to evaluate a candidate for the role of: **Junior Architect**\n\n---\nVACANCY REQUIREMENTS (reference):\n- Degree in architecture, interior design, or related field\n- Minimum 2 years experience in design and build\n- Software: AutoCAD, SketchUp, Revit (listed as examples,\n  not all mandatory)\n- Strong creative, visualization, and communication skills\n- Available to join ASAP\n\n---\nSTEP 0 — EDUCATION CHECK (run first, before scoring):\nVerify if candidate has or is pursuing a relevant degree\n(architecture, interior design, or closely related field).\n\nIMPORTANT: Evaluate the HIGHEST completed degree first.\n- If candidate has completed a relevant Bachelor's degree\n  OR higher → education_check = \"complete\", no penalty,\n  even if they are currently pursuing a Master's or PhD.\n- If candidate's ONLY relevant degree is still in progress\n  (no completed relevant degree yet) → education_check =\n  \"in_progress\", apply -5 to experience_match.\n- No relevant degree at all → education_check = \"not_relevant\",\n  cap skills_match at maximum 75.\n\n---\nEVALUATION PRINCIPLES:\n- Distinguish clearly between SKILLS and EXPERIENCE\n- EXPERIENCE levels:\n  - \"none\" = no evidence\n  - \"partial\" = indirect or supporting involvement\n  - \"strong\" = clear ownership or leadership\n- Count BOTH explicit and implicit evidence\n  Implicit evidence includes:\n  - coordination meetings\n  - collaboration with stakeholders\n  - monitoring projects\n  - site supervision\n  - working with contractors or engineers\n\n---\nSTRICT RULE:\nDo NOT assume ownership or responsibility unless explicitly stated.\nGeneral involvement, participation, or support tasks are NOT enough\nto qualify as end-to-end project experience.\n\n---\nEXPERIENCE RELEVANCE WEIGHTING:\nBefore scoring experience_match, classify the candidate's\nPRIMARY work experience into one relevance level:\n\nHIGH (full weight) — primary role involves:\n- Architectural or interior design work with creative input\n- Project involvement at architecture or design firms\n- Freelance architecture or interior projects with design decisions\n\nMEDIUM (70% weight) — primary role involves:\n- Drafting for architecture where candidate has some design input\n- Construction site supervision with design context\n\nLOW (30% weight) — primary role is:\n- Structural or geotechnical TESTING (load test, integrity test,\n  sensor monitoring), even if done on architectural projects\n- Pure 3D visualization or rendering only, with no design\n  decision-making involvement\n- Drafting that strictly executes others' designs with no\n  conceptual or spatial design input\n- QC or quality control roles\n\nMIXED — use when candidate has BOTH high AND low relevance:\n- Main job = low relevance (e.g. structural testing, pure drafter)\n  BUT also has meaningful high-relevance work on the side\n  (e.g. freelance architectural projects)\n- Do NOT classify as \"high\" just because there is some\n  architectural exposure in a low-relevance role\n- Classify as \"mixed\" and apply 50% weight to experience_match\n\nApply this relevance weight BEFORE calculating experience_match.\n\n---\nROLE-SPECIFIC RULES:\nFor Junior Architect:\n- Strong technical skills are HIGHLY valued\n- Partial experience is acceptable and expected\n- Lack of end-to-end project ownership is NORMAL and should\n  NOT heavily penalize the candidate\n- Focus on exposure, learning potential, and involvement\n  rather than leadership\n\nEnd-to-end project classification:\n- \"strong\" → clear ownership from start to finish\n- \"partial\" → strong involvement in multiple stages\n  with meaningful responsibility\n- \"none\" → no clear lifecycle involvement or ownership\n\n---\nCANDIDATE DATA:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json) }}\n\n---\nTASK:\n\n1. Run STEP 0 — education check\n\n2. Extract candidate email address from CV.\n   - If found, return the email as a string.\n   - If not found, return empty string \"\".\n\n3. Extract top SKILLS (max 10, prioritize relevant tools/software)\n\n4. TOOLS ASSESSMENT — apply before finalizing skills_match:\n   Vacancy mentions AutoCAD, SketchUp, Revit as examples,\n   not all mandatory. Assess as follows:\n   - Has AutoCAD + SketchUp + Revit → full score, no deduction\n   - Has AutoCAD + SketchUp (no Revit) → no penalty\n   - Has only one of the three → deduct 8 points from skills_match\n   - Has none of the three → deduct 15 points from skills_match\n\n5. Evaluate EXPERIENCE with relevance weighting applied:\n   - project_management\n   - vendor_coordination\n   - end_to_end_project\n   - relevance_level\n\n6. Calculate scores (0–100):\n   - skills_match (after tools assessment)\n   - experience_match (after relevance weighting\n     and education penalty if applicable)\n\nSCORING GUIDELINES:\n\nskills_match:\n- 85–100 → strong relevant tools including all required software\n- 70–84 → most required tools present, minor gaps\n- 50–69 → moderate relevance, missing key tools\n- <50 → weak or irrelevant\n\nexperience_match (after relevance weight applied):\n- 70–100 → multiple HIGH-relevance experiences,\n  clear and meaningful involvement\n- 50–69 → partial involvement in relevant tasks\n- 30–49 → mostly LOW or MIXED relevance experience\n- <30 → minimal or unrelated experience\n\nEXPERIENCE DURATION (supporting factor only):\n- 3+ years HIGH-relevance → add +5 to experience_match\n- 1–3 years HIGH-relevance → no adjustment\n- Mostly LOW-relevance regardless of duration → apply -5\n- Duration does NOT override relevance quality\n\n7. Apply final decision:\n\nDecision rules:\n- \"pass\":\n  skills_match ≥ 75 AND experience_match ≥ 20\n  AND has at least some relevant experience\n  (HIGH, MEDIUM, or MIXED relevance)\n\n- \"not_pass\":\n  skills_match < 60 regardless of experience\n  OR experience_match < 20 regardless of skills\n  OR relevance_level = \"low\" with experience_match < 30\n\n8. Write \"reason\" — follow